From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:42:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/25] [Worker] Optionally cap a worker's share of unified
 memory

vLLM never calls torch.cuda.set_per_process_memory_fraction. Both
gpu_memory_utilization and --kv-cache-memory-bytes size the KV pool
only; nothing bounds the allocations outside it, such as GLM-5.3's
sparse-indexer scores, which grow with chunk size x context / kpool. On
GB10's unified memory there is no separate VRAM to run out of first: an
overrun takes host memory until the node stops forking and its watchdog
resets it, and the OOM killer cannot reclaim a CUDA allocation.

VLLM_GLM53_MEM_FRACTION=<f> caps the worker's torch allocator at that
fraction of device memory right after the device is set, so an overrun
becomes torch.OutOfMemoryError: one request fails and the node keeps
serving. Unset (the default) changes nothing. Allocations that bypass
the torch allocator (NCCL, cuBLAS/FlashInfer workspaces) are not
covered.

Source: kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 @ c748079,
  image/patches/worker_memory_cap.py and spark_mem_trace.arm()
  (TORCH_MEM_FRACTION), by Matt Mastracci; porting authorized by the
  owner. The memory trace and reporter in spark_mem_trace are not
  ported.
Upstream: absent in v0.31.0 and main.
Claimed gain: stability only. Kindling runs with 0.92 on 4x GB10.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
index 1f34dfef8..d156acb66 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
@@ -460,6 +460,14 @@ class Worker(WorkerBase):
             )
             self.device = torch.device(f"cuda:{visible_device_index}")
             torch.accelerator.set_device_index(self.device)
+            # On unified memory (GB10) nothing bounds a worker's allocations
+            # outside the KV pool, and an overrun stalls the host instead of
+            # failing. This caps the torch allocator so it raises an OOM error;
+            # leave room for the weights, the KV pool and a prefill's scratch.
+            if mem_fraction := os.environ.get("VLLM_GLM53_MEM_FRACTION"):
+                torch.cuda.set_per_process_memory_fraction(
+                    float(mem_fraction), self.device
+                )
 
             current_platform.check_if_supports_dtype(self.model_config.dtype)
 
